<title>UK: Grandmet's Corbett leaves company.</title>
<headline>Grandmet's Corbett leaves company.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Grand Metropolitan Group Plc said on Thursday its finance director Gerald Corbett would leave the company today.</p>
<p>Corbett's resignation was anticipated at the time of the announcement of the proposed merger with Guinness Plc, GrandMet said.  </p>
<p>On May 12, GrandMet and Guinness announced their merger intentions, while adding both firms would have an equal number of people on the new entity's board.</p>
<p>It was envisaged at the time that Guinness's Philip Yea would become group finance director of the merged company.</p>
<p>&quot;Gerald (Corbett) has played a major role, not only in the merger, but in getting GrandMet to the good position we have today,&quot; GrandMet chairman George Bull said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 652 7717</p>
